design:
Favor breadth at level 1 over advancement. The validator should cover the choice families named in the epic, but test fixtures can use a compact subset of real ORC mechanical records. Derived output should include base ancestry/class/background names, level, HP, ability scores, proficiency summary, feats, equipment, and spells when the selected class uses them.

Initial test sketch:
```ts
const result = completeCharacterCreation(dbWithPathfinderCampaign(), {
  draft: validPathfinderDraft(),
  sessionId: 's1',
  at: now,
});
expect(result.ok).toBe(true);
expect(readCharacter(db).class_name).toBe('Fighter');
expect(JSON.parse(readCharacter(db).ability_scores_json).strength).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(16);
```
